algolia_search.js
```js
search.addWidget(
    instantsearch.widgets.searchBox({
      container: '.pw_st_search_search',
      placeholder: '',
    })
  );
```
in php template:
```html
<script>
    var client = algoliasearch('correct key', 'correct api');
    var index = client.initIndex('correct index');
    autocomplete('.pw_st_search_search',
    { hint: true }, {
    source: autocomplete.sources.hits(index, {hitsPerPage: 5}),
    displayKey: 'name',
    templates: {
        suggestion: function(suggestion) {
          //console.log(suggestion);
          return '<span>' + suggestion._highlightResult.name.value + '</span><span>';
        }
    }
});
</script>
```
I cant show you our original input because it is too dynamically generated but with this input is the same issue:
```html
<div class="aa-input-container" id="aa-input-container">
      <input type="search" id="" class=".pw_st_search_search aa-input-search" placeholder="Search " name="search" autocomplete="on" />
</div>
```

Hmm i make it work but i don't know why ;). I move this part to our header, and autocomplete start working.
```
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/algoliasearch/3/algoliasearch.min.js"></script>
	 <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/autocomplete.js/0/autocomplete.min.js"></script>
	 <script>
		var client = algoliasearch('NNWYKHZ90Y', 'd052c2a715d25707636e3a29d145e9e9');
		var index = client.initIndex('prod_query_suggestions');
		autocomplete('.pw_st_search_search',
		{ hint: true }, {
		source: autocomplete.sources.hits(index, {hitsPerPage: 5}),
		displayKey: 'query',
		templates: {
			suggestion: function(suggestion) {
			  console.log(suggestion);
			  return '<span>' + suggestion._highlightResult.query.value + '</span>';
			}
			}
		});
	</script>
```
But search box stop working. Then I change widget container to another class of input like this:
```
search.addWidget(
    instantsearch.widgets.searchBox({
      container: '.aa-input',
      placeholder: '',
    })
  );
```
And now work autocomplete and searching simultaneously
